The proof strategy is now fixed: execute both program-defined bodies under the supplied semantics, use circularities for the unbounded coefficient fold and both unbounded bisection loops, and constrain the result to an exact recursive summary of those executions. This covers arbitrary finite mixed integer/float coefficient lists; the fixed float primitives remain the only conditional trust boundary.
