The first residual exposed a real invariant-shape issue: an abstract local-map remainder allowed impossible closure-cell frames. I’m making the helper’s local frame syntactically stable by initializing `coeff` before the loop, then pinning the exact plain-function locals in the circularity. This does not change the polynomial result.
