The whole-program residual is the known Haskell-backend gap for a ground float negation. I’m avoiding a proof-only execution shortcut: the code now derives the same concrete endpoints from the guaranteed nonzero list length, keeping the fixed `divII` primitive symbolic during proof and concrete under LLVM. The formal result summary is updated to those exact endpoint terms.
