The loop circularities themselves are now closing, but the whole-entry proof is still descending into fixed float hooks before reusing the established loop theorem. I’m applying the Kit’s permitted connection-theorem pattern: compile the circularities against a bridge-free base, then add one exact-context bridge whose left/right configurations are identical to the already-proved expansion-loop theorem. The proof records will keep those two builds separate.
