The isolation result is diagnostic, not a failed target: the bisection claim invokes `poly`, so selecting it without the three coefficient-fold lemmas intentionally leaves an arbitrary iterator stuck. I’m rerunning it with those required lemmas enabled, then I’ll isolate only the expansion-to-bisection handoff.
